inge, which is highly beneficial for note-taking and creative tasks. While the MacBook Air offers the best performance-per-watt, the Windows options provide greater software compatibility for specific engineering or specialized academic applications.\", \"first_step\": \"\", \"steps\": [], \"steps_title\": \"\", \"difficulty\": \"\", \"category\": \"\", \"product\": null, \"accessory\": null, \"video_url\": \"\", \"safety\": \"\", \"suggestions\": [], \"ai\": true, \"notice\": \"\", \"mentioned_products\": []}}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"text\": \"show those products\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"answer\": {\"kind\": \"answer\", \"badge\": \"AI answer\", \"title\": \"Student Laptop Product Comparison\", \"summary\": \"The MacBook Air (M2/M3) features an aluminum unibody design with a Liquid Retina display, starting at approximately $899-$1,099 depending on the configuration. The Dell XPS 13 is a premium Windows ultrabook known for its InfinityEdge display and CNC-machined aluminum chassis, typically priced between $1,000 and $1,400. The Lenovo Yoga 7i is a versatile 2-in-1 convertible with a 360-degree hinge and touchscreen, usually retailing between $750 and $1,000. These models represent the top tier of student computing, balancing portability with the necessary processing power for academic software.\", \"first_step\": \"\", \"steps\": [], \"steps_title\": \"\", \"difficulty\": \"\", \"category\": \"\", \"product\": null, \"accessory\": null, \"video_url\": \"\", \"safety\": \"\", \"suggestions\": [], \"ai\": true, \"notice\": \"\", \"mentioned_products\": []}}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"text\": \"MacBook Air (M2/M3)\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"answer\": {\"kind\": \"fallback\", \"badge\": \"No exact match\", \"title\": \"MacBook Air M2 and M3 Overview\", \"summary\": \"The MacBook Air M2 and M3 are Apple\'s current thin-and-light laptop offerings, both featuring the iconic fanless design, Liquid Retina displays, and MagSafe 3 charging. The M2 model uses the 5nm 