p 3: Check Task Manager for runaway processes. Step 4: Use a cooling pad. Step 5: Re-paste CPU/GPU and replace thermal pads if temps stay above 95C (service center).','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFkEM_8ylwY','2026-10-16 05:32:57.021000','2026-10-16 05:32:57.021000',4,246),(236,'WiFi keeps disconnecting — HP OMEN Transcend 14 OLED','[HP HP OMEN Transcend 14 OLED] WiFi drops randomly while other devices stay connected.','Step 1: Forget the network and reconnect. Step 2: Update the WiFi driver from the maker site. Step 3: In Device Manager, disable \'allow computer to turn off this device\' for the WiFi adapter. Step 4: Switch between 2.4GHz and 5GHz bands. Step 5: Reset network stack (netsh winsock reset).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9xHAl51uRl0','2026-10-16 05:32:57.035000','2026-10-16 05:32:57.037000',4,246),(237,'Very slow boot / Windows sluggish — HP Victus 15 RTX 4050','[HP HP Victus 15 RTX 4050] Takes minutes to boot; apps lag and freeze.','Step 1: Disable unnecessary Startup apps in Task Manager. Step 2: Free disk space (min 15% free). Step 3: Run antivirus/malware scan. Step 4: Upgrade to SSD and add RAM if still on HDD/4GB. Step 5: Reinstall Windows as a last resort after backup.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CcFY5GTdbIk','2026-10-16 05:32:57.132000','2026-10-16 05:32:57.132000',4,247),(238,'Screen flickering — HP Victus 15 RTX 4050','[HP HP Victus 15 RTX 4050] Display flickers, flashes, or shows lines.','Step 1: Update display and GPU drivers. Step 2: Test with an external monitor to isolate panel vs GPU. Step 3: Change refresh rate to the panel default (60/120/144Hz). Step 4: Check the display cable if flicker changes with lid angle. Step 5: Replace panel/cable at service if hardware-side.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0SyTT7tvb0U','2026-10-16 05:32:57.144000','2026-10-16 05:32:57.144000',4,247),(239,'Some keyboard keys not working — HP Victus 16 RTX 5060','[HP HP Victus 16 RTX 5060] Certain keys type not