4,411),(310,'No sound from speakers — LG Gram 16 (2024)','[LG LG Gram 16 (2024)] Videos play but no audio from built-in speakers.','Step 1: Check volume mixer and that the right output is selected. Step 2: Unplug HDMI/Bluetooth devices that may hijack audio. Step 3: Reinstall audio driver from maker site. Step 4: Run the built-in audio troubleshooter. Step 5: Test with earphones to isolate speaker hardware.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HXGiSv75yis','2026-10-16 05:33:01.111000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.111000',4,411),(311,'Blue screen / random crashes — LG Gram 14 (2024)','[LG LG Gram 14 (2024)] BSOD errors or sudden restarts under load.','Step 1: Note the stop code and failing driver file. Step 2: Update GPU/chipset drivers and Windows. Step 3: Run memory test (mdsched) and disk check (chkdsk). Step 4: Stress-test thermals; overheating causes crashes. Step 5: Back up data and reinstall OS; service board/RAM if it persists.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wTuyfgoTJJo','2026-10-16 05:33:01.211000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.211000',4,412),(312,'Touchpad not responding — LG Gram 14 (2024)','[LG LG Gram 14 (2024)] Cursor frozen or touchpad gestures dead.','Step 1: Press the touchpad toggle key (Fn+F-key). Step 2: Check Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Touchpad is enabled. Step 3: Reinstall precision touchpad driver. Step 4: Test in BIOS to rule out software. Step 5: Reseat/replace the touchpad ribbon cable at service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7dzP0Zx-2s','2026-10-16 05:33:01.223000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.223000',4,412),(313,'Laptop won\'t turn on — Razer Blade 14 (2024)','[Razer Razer Blade 14 (2024)] Pressing power does nothing; no lights or fan spin.','Step 1: Hold power 15s to force-drain. Step 2: Unplug all USB devices and charger. Step 3: Plug the original charger, wait 10 mins, try again. Step 4: Reseat battery if removable. Step 5: Try a known-good charger. Step 6: Bring to service if still dead (possible board issue).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=apm_gDfvicU','2026-10-16 05:33:01.294000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.294000',4,413),(314,'Battery drains too fast — Razer Blade 14 (2024)','[Razer Razer Blade 14 (2024)] Battery drops quickly even on light use.','Step 1: Lower brightness to 50% and enable Battery Saver. Step 2: Check battery usage in Settings, close background hogs. Step 3: Update BIOS and drivers. Step 4: Generate battery report (powercfg /batteryreport) and check wear. Step 5: Replace battery if wear exceeds 30%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MCUa3-I7B0c','2026-10-16 05:33:01.305000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.305000',4,413),(315,'Laptop overheats / fan very loud — Razer Blade 16 (2024)','[Razer Razer Blade 16 (2024)] Hot chassis, loud fans, sudden slowdowns or shutdowns.','Step 1: Use on a hard flat surface (not bed/pillow). Step 2: Clean vents with compressed air. Step 3: Check Task Manager for runaway processes. Step 4: Use a cooling pad. Step 5: Re-paste CPU/GPU and replace thermal pads if temps stay above 95C (service center).','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v5hMU5ZHaCY','2026-10-16 05:33:01.405000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.405000',4,414),(316,'WiFi keeps disconnecting — Razer Blade 16 (2024)','[Razer Razer Blade 16 (2024)] WiFi drops randomly while other devices stay connected.','Step 1: Forget the network and reconnect. Step 2: Update the WiFi driver from the maker site. Step 3: In Device Manager, disable \'allow computer to turn off this device\' for the WiFi adapter. Step 4: Switch between 2.4GHz and 5GHz bands. Step 5: Reset network stack (netsh winsock reset).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G4PA5-ysj4g','2026-10-16 05:33:01.414000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.414000',4,414),(317,'Very slow boot / Windows sluggish — Gigabyte G5 KF5','[Gigabyte Gigabyte G5 KF5] Takes minutes to boot; apps lag and freeze.','Step 1: Disable unnecessary Startup apps in Task Manager. Step 2: Free disk space (min 15% free). Step 3: Run antivirus/malware scan. Step 4: Upgrade to