iver file. Step 2: Update GPU/chipset drivers and Windows. Step 3: Run memory test (mdsched) and disk check (chkdsk). Step 4: Stress-test thermals; overheating causes crashes. Step 5: Back up data and reinstall OS; service board/RAM if it persists.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wTuyfgoTJJo','2026-10-16 05:33:01.668000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.668000',4,417),(322,'Touchpad not responding — Xiaomi RedmiBook 15 (2024)','[Xiaomi Xiaomi RedmiBook 15 (2024)] Cursor frozen or touchpad gestures dead.','Step 1: Press the touchpad toggle key (Fn+F-key). Step 2: Check Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Touchpad is enabled. Step 3: Reinstall precision touchpad driver. Step 4: Test in BIOS to rule out software. Step 5: Reseat/replace the touchpad ribbon cable at service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5xvCee9wNvQ','2026-10-16 05:33:01.680000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.680000',4,417),(323,'Laptop won\'t turn on — Xiaomi Book 14 (2024)','[Xiaomi Xiaomi Book 14 (2024)] Pressing power does nothing; no lights or fan spin.','Step 1: Hold power 15s to force-drain. Step 2: Unplug all USB devices and charger. Step 3: Plug the original charger, wait 10 mins, try again. Step 4: Reseat battery if removable. Step 5: Try a known-good charger. Step 6: Bring to service if still dead (possible board issue).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFZUZqveQp4','2026-10-16 05:33:01.794000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.794000',4,418),(324,'Battery drains too fast — Xiaomi Book 14 (2024)','[Xiaomi Xiaomi Book 14 (2024)] Battery drops quickly even on light use.','Step 1: Lower brightness to 50% and enable Battery Saver. Step 2: Check battery usage in Settings, close background hogs. Step 3: Update BIOS and drivers. Step 4: Generate battery report (powercfg /batteryreport) and check wear. Step 5: Replace battery if wear exceeds 30%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=STktToXWeVw','2026-10-16 05:33:01.794000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.794000',4,418),(325,'Laptop overheats / fan very loud — Google Pixelbook Go','[Google Google Pixelbook Go] Hot chassis, loud fans, sudden slowdowns or shutdowns.','Step 1: Use on a hard flat surface (not bed/pillow). Step 2: Clean vents with compressed air. Step 3: Check Task Manager for runaway processes. Step 4: Use a cooling pad. Step 5: Re-paste CPU/GPU and replace thermal pads if temps stay above 95C (service center).','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFkEM_8ylwY','2026-10-16 05:33:01.922000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.922000',4,419),(326,'WiFi keeps disconnecting — Google Pixelbook Go','[Google Google Pixelbook Go] WiFi drops randomly while other devices stay connected.','Step 1: Forget the network and reconnect. Step 2: Update the WiFi driver from the maker site. Step 3: In Device Manager, disable \'allow computer to turn off this device\' for the WiFi adapter. Step 4: Switch between 2.4GHz and 5GHz bands. Step 5: Reset network stack (netsh winsock reset).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCjHC-jJc0A','2026-10-16 05:33:01.935000','2026-10-16 05:33:01.935000',4,419),(327,'Fix Apple iPhone 6 (2014): Battery drains quickly','The Apple iPhone 6 (2014) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xznJvO7JVXY','2026-10-17 13:17:25.470000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.470000',4,420),(328,'Fix Apple iPhone 6s Plus (2015): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The Apple iPhone 6s Plus (2015) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3NnwNpMhtUk','2026-10-17 13:17:25.486000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.486000',4,421),(329,'Fix Apple iPad Air 2 (2014): Will not charge past 1%','The Apple iPad Air 2 (2014) plugs in but the battery icon stays at 0-1 percent or shows a charging error.','1. Clean the charging port with a wooden pick and compressed air.\n2. Try a different cable and at least a 2A adapter.\n3. Leave it connected to power for 30 minutes before trying to boot.\n4. An inflated or dead battery must be replaced professionally.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-_J5y7UCCY','2026-10-17 13:17:25.502000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.502000',4,422),(330,'Fix Apple iPad mini 2 (2013): Touchscreen not responding','Taps and swipes on the Apple iPad mini 2 (2013) are ignored, mostly after a fall.','1. Force restart and hold Power + Home for 15 seconds.\n2. Remove any screen protector that may be lifting.\n3. Test the screen in Safe Mode.\n4. Replace the digitiser if dead zones remain.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w80due1ifSM','2026-10-17 13:17:25.527000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.527000',4,423),(331,'Fix Apple MacBook Pro 13-inch Mid 2012: Not charging / no power light','The Apple MacBook Pro 13-inch Mid 2012 shows no charging LED and does not power on with the adapter connected.','1. Test the adapter on another laptop and check the pin for damage.\n2. Unplug the battery, hold Power for 30 seconds, then reconnect everything.\n3. Try a different wall outlet and inspect the DC jack for looseness.\n4. A loose jack or dead board needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r6a-RPrrAn4','2026-10-17 13:17:25.553000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.553000',4,424),(332,'Fix Apple MacBook Air 11-inch Early 2015: Fan noise and overheating','The Apple MacBook Air 11-inch Early 2015 runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wvUXJQ2UiVw','2026-10-17 13:17:25.577000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.577000',4,425),(333,'Fix Apple Watch Series 1 (2016): Will not pair with the phone','The Apple Watch Series 1 (2016) cannot be found in Bluetooth settings or pairing always fails.','1. Turn Bluetooth off and on again on the phone, then restart the watch.\n2. Forget the device and delete its app data, then pair from scratch.\n3. Update the companion app and the watch firmware.\n4. Factory reset the watch if it still will not connect.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NGa0-VsyuEc','2026-10-17 13:17:25.593000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.593000',4,426),(334,'Fix Apple AirPods 1st generation (2016): Sound only in one ear','One side of the Apple AirPods 1st generation (2016) is silent or cuts in and out when the cable moves.','1. Clean the driver mesh and ear tips of wax and debris.\n2. Test another device to confirm the fault follows the earbuds.\n3. On wired models, bend the cable near the jack - a drop means a broken wire.\n4. For true wireless, put both buds in the case and reset them.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mq_8jlg4skA','2026-10-17 13:17:25.618000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.618000',4,427),(335,'Fix Apple TV HD (2015): Sound but no picture','The Apple TV HD (2015) plays audio but the screen stays black or very dim.','1. Cover the room - an image may be visible, pointing to backlight failure.\n2. Reseat the HDMI cable and switch to another input.\n3. Unplug the TV for 60 seconds, then power it on again.\n4. A dead backlight strip needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRRjK7ItKKM','2026-10-17 13:17:25.635000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.635000',4,428),(336,'Fix Apple iMac 21.5-inch Late 2013: Powers on but no display','The Apple iMac 21.5-inch Late 2013 fans spin and lights come on, but the monitor stays black.','1. Reseat the RAM and the graphics card.\n2. Try a different video cable and input on the monitor.\n3. Clear CMOS by removing the battery for five minutes.\n4. Listen for beep codes - they identify the failed component.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c4q19q3grc4','2026-10-17 13:17:25.652000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.652000',4,429),(337,'Fix Samsung Galaxy S5 (2014): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the Samsung Galaxy S5 (2014) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S_jEB7S9FzE','2026-10-17 13:17:25.668000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.668000',4,430),(338,'Fix Samsung Galaxy Note 4 (2014): Overheating while charging','The Samsung Galaxy Note 4 (2014) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FRkI0w8AITQ','2026-10-17 13:17:25.688000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.688000',4,431),(339,'Fix Samsung Galaxy S III (2012): Battery drains quickly','The Samsung Galaxy S III (2012) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jbGgoiqhvfE','2026-10-17 13:17:25.709000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.709000',4,432),(340,'Fix Samsung Galaxy J7 (2016): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The Samsung Galaxy J7 (2016) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pwhGfnaqd3k','2026-10-17 13:17:25.725000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.725000',4,433),(341,'Fix Samsung Galaxy S8 (2017): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the Samsung Galaxy S8 (2017) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k-Q_s2COeZs','2026-10-17 13:17:25.749000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.749000',4,434),(342,'Fix Samsung Galaxy Tab A 9.7 (2015): Wi-Fi keeps disconnecting','The Samsung Galaxy Tab A 9.7 (2015) drops the Wi-Fi connection while other devices stay online.','1. Forget the network, reboot the router and reconnect.\n2. Set the router channel manually to 1, 6 or 11.\n3. Reset network settings on the tablet.\n4. Install system updates - many old tablets shipped with buggy Wi-Fi firmware.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ljQfo-uBTDg','2026-10-17 13:17:25.766000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.766000',4,435),(343,'Fix Samsung SyncMaster S22B350 (2012): Monitor stays black','The Samsung SyncMaster S22B350 (2012) powers on with an LED but shows no picture at all.','1. Press the input/source button to select the correct input.\n2. Reseat the video cable at both ends and try another cable.\n3. Test the monitor on another PC or plug in a different display.\n4. A dead power board or backlight needs repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2JVjHZ1QPL4','2026-10-17 13:17:25.791000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.791000',4,436),(344,'Fix Samsung Gear S2 (2015): Battery no longer holds a charge','The Samsung Gear S2 (2015) runs for less than a few hours and dies before the end of the day.','1. Reduce screen brightness and disable always-on display.\n2. Turn off 24/7 heart rate monitoring and GPS when unused.\n3. Clean the charging pins and reseat it on the dock.\n4. Batteries age - replace the unit or cell if capacity is below 60%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zCRdJmFIBJk','2026-10-17 13:17:25.808000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.808000',4,437),(345,'Fix Samsung Galaxy Buds (2019): Will not hold a charge','The Samsung Galaxy Buds (2019) dies within minutes even after a full charge cycle.','1. Clean the charging contacts with a dry cotton swab.\n2. Leave it on charge for 30 minutes before use and use a 5V adapter.\n3. Update the firmware from the companion app.\n4. Old cells fade - battery replacement or a new unit is the fix.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Xynrkw61uM','2026-10-17 13:17:25.824000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.824000',4,438),(346,'Fix Samsung UN40H6350 Smart TV (2014): Apps freeze or crash','Apps on the Samsung UN40H6350 Smart TV (2014) hang, crash back to the home screen or never load.','1. Clear the app cache and data from settings.\n2. Uninstall and reinstall the failing app.\n3. Update the TV firmware from Settings > Support.\n4. As a last resort, reset the TV to factory settings.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J6_TBoMpFIc','2026-10-17 13:17:25.852000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.852000',4,439),(347,'Fix Xiaomi Mi 4 (2014): Overheating while charging','The Xiaomi Mi 4 (2014) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-OhrHa9fiM','2026-10-17 13:17:25.869000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.869000',4,440),(348,'Fix Xiaomi Redmi Note 3 (2016): Battery drains quickly','The Xiaomi Redmi Note 3 (2016) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uiwkwjJtvWI','2026-10-17 13:17:25.883000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.883000',4,441),(349,'Fix Xiaomi Redmi 4X (2017): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The Xiaomi Redmi 4X (2017) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JQWMCeM0NhE','2026-10-17 13:17:25.904000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.904000',4,442),(350,'Fix Xiaomi Mi A1 (2017): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the Xiaomi Mi A1 (2017) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NGQtC8WWX7c','2026-10-17 13:17:25.921000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.921000',4,443),(351,'Fix Xiaomi Mi 8 (2018): Overheating while charging','The Xiaomi Mi 8 (2018) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K0mW09uT4mo','2026-10-17 13:17:25.938000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.938000',4,444),(352,'Fix Xiaomi Mi Band 2 (2016): Charger not recognised','The Xiaomi Mi Band 2 (2016) does not light up or charge on its original dock.','1. Clean the magnetic contacts and pins with a dry cloth.\n2. Try a different USB cable and a phone charger, not a laptop port.\n3. Reset the watch while it is on the charger.\n4. Replace the dock if the cable tests fine elsewhere.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H7oXU8CqjXk','2026-10-17 13:17:25.950000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.950000',4,445),(353,'Fix Xiaomi Redmi AirDots (2019): Pairing fails or drops','The Xiaomi Redmi AirDots (2019) disappears from the device list or will not complete pairing.','1. Forget the device on the phone, then restart both devices.\n2. Clear the pairing list on the headphones and pair again.\n3. Move away from Wi-Fi routers and USB 3.0 hubs that cause interference.\n4. Update the app and firmware to the latest version.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UEPtExkxV4o','2026-10-17 13:17:25.966000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.966000',4,446),(354,'Fix Xiaomi Mi Router 3C (2017): No internet but Wi-Fi is connected','Devices join the Xiaomi Mi Router 3C (2017) network but pages will not load.','1. Restart the modem and the router in that order.\n2. Check that the WAN cable is plugged into the correct port.\n3. Release and renew the IP address on the affected device.\n4. Reset the router to factory defaults if the modem line is fine.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1WVFI3W6Sfk','2026-10-17 13:17:25.983000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.983000',4,447),(355,'Fix Xiaomi Mi TV 4A 43-inch (2018): Cannot connect to Wi-Fi','The Xiaomi Mi TV 4A 43-inch (2018) will not see or join the home wireless network.','1. Restart the router and move it closer to the TV.\n2. Forget the network on the TV and re-enter the password.\n3. Set the router to 2.4GHz - many older TVs do not see 5GHz.\n4. Reset network settings on the TV if the password is correct.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dI5BaGERcKA','2026-10-17 13:17:25.999000','2026-10-17 13:17:25.999000',4,448),(356,'Fix Xiaomi Mi Notebook Air 13.3 (2016): Extremely slow boot and apps','The Xiaomi Mi Notebook Air 13.3 (2016) takes many minutes to boot and applications hang constantly.','1. Run Disk Cleanup and remove startup programs you do not need.\n2. Check Task Manager for a drive stuck at 100 percent use.\n3. Scan for malware with up-to-date antivirus software.\n4. The biggest fix on older laptops is swapping the HDD for an SSD.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CcFY5GTdbIk','2026-10-17 13:17:26.017000','2026-10-17 13:17:26.017000',4,449),(357,'Fix Huawei Ascend P7 (2014): Battery drains quickly','The Huawei Ascend P7 (2014) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N3qLj5Sl2z0','2026-10-17 13:17:26.033000','2026-10-17 13:17:26.033000',4,450),(358,'Fix Huawei Mate 7 (2014): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The Huawei Mate 7 (2014) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube