an, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZNEbr_E0Wr0','2026-10-17 13:17:26.171000','2026-10-17 13:17:26.171000',4,455),(363,'Fix Huawei MediaPad M3 (2016): Will not charge past 1%','The Huawei MediaPad M3 (2016) plugs in but the battery icon stays at 0-1 percent or shows a charging error.','1. Clean the charging port with a wooden pick and compressed air.\n2. Try a different cable and at least a 2A adapter.\n3. Leave it connected to power for 30 minutes before trying to boot.\n4. An inflated or dead battery must be replaced professionally.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=09zn_WbJ-mE','2026-10-17 13:17:26.202000','2026-10-17 13:17:26.202000',4,456),(364,'Fix Huawei Watch GT (2018): Will not pair with the phone','The Huawei Watch GT (2018) cannot be found in Bluetooth settings or pairing always fails.','1. Turn Bluetooth off and on again on the phone, then restart the watch.\n2. Forget the device and delete its app data, then pair from scratch.\n3. Update the companion app and the watch firmware.\n4. Factory reset the watch if it still will not connect.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jpOjzaOpH10','2026-10-17 13:17:26.229000','2026-10-17 13:17:26.229000',4,457),(365,'Fix Huawei FreeBuds 3 (2019): Distortion at higher volume','The Huawei FreeBuds 3 (2019) crackles or sounds muffled when the volume goes up.','1. Lower the source volume and disable any equaliser boosts.\n2. Clean the speaker grille and check for a torn driver surround.\n3. Test on a second device to confirm it is not the source.\n4. A blown driver needs replacement.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u4vjJi35HbM','2026-10-17 13:17:26.243000','2026-10-17 13:17:26.243000',4,458),(366,'Fix Huawei MateBook D (2018): Keyboard or trackpad not responding','Some keys on the Huawei MateBook D (2018) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with comp