d the watch firmware.\n4. Factory reset the watch if it still will not connect.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HytYYJdg9B0','2026-10-17 13:17:27.724000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.724000',4,538),(446,'Fix HONOR Magic Earbuds (2020): Distortion at higher volume','The HONOR Magic Earbuds (2020) crackles or sounds muffled when the volume goes up.','1. Lower the source volume and disable any equaliser boosts.\n2. Clean the speaker grille and check for a torn driver surround.\n3. Test on a second device to confirm it is not the source.\n4. A blown driver needs replacement.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gOkNaw_LBnU','2026-10-17 13:17:27.742000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.742000',4,539),(447,'Fix ASUS Zenfone 2 (2015): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the ASUS Zenfone 2 (2015) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ncUNKtpSxpw','2026-10-17 13:17:27.760000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.760000',4,540),(448,'Fix ASUS Zenfone 5 (2014): Overheating while charging','The ASUS Zenfone 5 (2014) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ps9AgwCUY94','2026-10-17 13:17:27.782000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.782000',4,541),(449,'Fix ASUS Zenfone Max Pro M1 (2018): Battery drains quickly','The ASUS Zenfone Max Pro M1 (2018) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2.