: Fan noise and overheating','The ASUS ZenBook UX305 (2015) runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFkEM_8ylwY','2026-10-17 13:17:27.896000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.896000',4,546),(454,'Fix ASUS ROG Strix GL502 (2016): Extremely slow boot and apps','The ASUS ROG Strix GL502 (2016) takes many minutes to boot and applications hang constantly.','1. Run Disk Cleanup and remove startup programs you do not need.\n2. Check Task Manager for a drive stuck at 100 percent use.\n3. Scan for malware with up-to-date antivirus software.\n4. The biggest fix on older laptops is swapping the HDD for an SSD.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yvwuzE3uFIs','2026-10-17 13:17:27.912000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.912000',4,547),(455,'Fix ASUS VN247H (2014): Flickering or unstable image','The ASUS VN247H (2014) blinks, shows horizontal lines or loses sync randomly.','1. Swap in a known-good cable - cheap HDMI leads cause most flicker.\n2. Lower the refresh rate to 60Hz and disable adaptive sync.\n3. Update the graphics driver and remove overclocked display modes.\n4. Persistent flicker with a new cable means the panel is failing.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7iuniL5OgY','2026-10-17 13:17:27.937000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.937000',4,548),(456,'Fix ASUS ZenWatch 2 (2015): Battery no longer holds a charge','The ASUS ZenWatch 2 (2015) runs for less than a few hours and dies before the end of the day.','1. Reduce screen brightness and disable always-on display.\n2. Turn off 24/7 heart rate monitoring and GPS when unused.\n3. Clean the charging pins and reseat it on the dock.\n4. Batteries age - replace the unit or cell if capacity is below 60%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qHII3NF4CWw','2026-10-17 13:17:27.953000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.953000',4,549),(457,'Fix Acer Aspire V3-571G (2012): Keyboard or trackpad not responding','Some keys on the Acer Aspire V3-571G (2012) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with compressed air.\n2. Reinstall or update the touchpad and chipset drivers.\n3. Plug in an external keyboard to see if the fault is hardware.\n4. Replace the keyboard assembly if keys stay dead.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnOYqyonQqk','2026-10-17 13:17:27.969000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.969000',4,550),(458,'Fix Acer Aspire E5-573G (2015): Not charging / no power light','The Acer Aspire E5-573G (2015) shows no charging LED and does not power on with the adapter connected.','1. Test the adapter on another laptop and check the pin for damage.\n2. Unplug the battery, hold Power for 30 seconds, then reconnect everything.\n3. Try a different wall outlet and inspect the DC jack for looseness.\n4. A loose jack or dead board needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UYRsi0bY5GQ','2026-10-17 13:17:27.986000','2026-10-17 13:17:27.986000',4,551),(459,'Fix Acer Chromebook 14 (2016): Fan noise and overheating','The Acer Chromebook 14 (2016) runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFkEM_8ylwY','2026-10-17 13:17:28.011000','2026-10-17 13:17:28.011000',4,552),(460,'Fix Acer Iconia B1-720 (2014): Will not charge past 1%','The Acer Iconia B1-720 (2014) plugs in but the battery icon stays at 0-1 percent or shows a charging error.','1. Clean the charging port with a wooden pick and compressed air.\n2. Try a different cable and at least a 2A adapter.\n3. Leave it connected to power f