ght use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DP1EOYPWKb4','2026-10-17 13:17:28.382000','2026-10-17 13:17:28.382000',4,569),(477,'Fix HP Pavilion g6 (2012): Keyboard or trackpad not responding','Some keys on the HP Pavilion g6 (2012) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with compressed air.\n2. Reinstall or update the touchpad and chipset drivers.\n3. Plug in an external keyboard to see if the fault is hardware.\n4. Replace the keyboard assembly if keys stay dead.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CTqPL_kICbE','2026-10-17 13:17:28.411000','2026-10-17 13:17:28.411000',4,570),(478,'Fix HP Envy 15 (2012): Not charging / no power light','The HP Envy 15 (2012) shows no charging LED and does not power on with the adapter connected.','1. Test the adapter on another laptop and check the pin for damage.\n2. Unplug the battery, hold Power for 30 seconds, then reconnect everything.\n3. Try a different wall outlet and inspect the DC jack for looseness.\n4. A loose jack or dead board needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MgDy0h9a7Jg','2026-10-17 13:17:28.427000','2026-10-17 13:17:28.427000',4,571),(479,'Fix HP EliteBook 840 G1 (2014): Fan noise and overheating','The HP EliteBook 840 G1 (2014) runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vpe1Sx28Mxg','2026-10-17 13:17:28.441000','2026-10-17 