n the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kXfvzG1414Q','2026-10-17 13:17:29.095000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.095000',4,603),(511,'Fix Google Pixel 2 (2017): Overheating while charging','The Google Pixel 2 (2017) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eMoR99X9ico','2026-10-17 13:17:29.128000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.128000',4,604),(512,'Fix Google Pixel C (2015): Touchscreen not responding','Taps and swipes on the Google Pixel C (2015) are ignored, mostly after a fall.','1. Force restart and hold Power + Home for 15 seconds.\n2. Remove any screen protector that may be lifting.\n3. Test the screen in Safe Mode.\n4. Replace the digitiser if dead zones remain.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kHbE7oL67DY','2026-10-17 13:17:29.151000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.151000',4,605),(513,'Fix Google Pixelbook (2017): Keyboard or trackpad not responding','Some keys on the Google Pixelbook (2017) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with compressed air.\n2. Reinstall or update the touchpad and chipset drivers.\n3. Plug in an external keyboard to see if the fault is hardware.\n4. Replace the keyboard assembly if keys stay dead.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kHAmlPLT5M4','2026-10-17 13:17:29.176000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.176000',4,606),(514,'Fix Google Pixel Buds 1st generation (2017): Sound only in one ear','One side of the Google Pixel Buds 1st generation (2017) is silent or cuts in and out when the cable moves.','1. Clean the driver mesh and ear tips of