4 (2015) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ulbyVgsbmes','2026-10-17 13:17:29.284000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.284000',4,611),(519,'Fix LG G5 (2016): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the LG G5 (2016) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z274bXPanN0','2026-10-17 13:17:29.302000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.302000',4,612),(520,'Fix LG K10 (2016): Overheating while charging','The LG K10 (2016) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7d0Umf4ZKs','2026-10-17 13:17:29.321000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.321000',4,613),(521,'Fix LG Spirit (2015): Battery drains quickly','The LG Spirit (2015) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RpK81wJD1pQ','2026-10-17 13:17:29.334000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.334000',4,614),(522,'Fix LG G Pad 7.0 (2014): Wi-Fi keeps disconnecting','The LG G Pad 7.0 (2014) drops the Wi-Fi connection while other devices stay online.','1. Forget the network, reboot the router and reconnect.\n2. Set the router channel manually to 1, 6 or 11.\n3. Reset network settings on the tablet.\n4. Install system updates - many old tablets shipped with buggy Wi-Fi firmware.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-n1J3h8vg1E','2026-10-17 13:17:29.360000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.360000',4,615),(523,'Fix LG Watch Urbane (2015): Will not pair with the phone','The LG Watch Urbane (2015) cannot be found in Bluetooth settings or pairing always fails.','1. Turn Bluetooth off and on again on the phone, then restart the watch.\n2. Forget the device and delete its app data, then pair from scratch.\n3. Update the companion app and the watch firmware.\n4. Factory reset the watch if it still will not connect.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ucz2xjsjlAE','2026-10-17 13:17:29.378000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.378000',4,616),(524,'Fix LG TONE Pro HBS-750 (2014): Pairing fails or drops','The LG TONE Pro HBS-750 (2014) disappears from the device list or will not complete pairing.','1. Forget the device on the phone, then restart both devices.\n2. Clear the pairing list on the headphones and pair again.\n3. Move away from Wi-Fi routers and USB 3.0 hubs that cause interference.\n4. Update the app and firmware to the latest version.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IDCWCBiczK8','2026-10-17 13:17:29.393000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.393000',4,617),(525,'Fix LG 42LN5400 (2013): Sound but no picture','The LG 42LN5400 (2013) plays audio but the screen stays black or very dim.','1. Cover the room - an image may be visible, pointing to backlight failure.\n2. Reseat the HDMI cable and switch to another input.\n3. Unplug the TV for 60 seconds, then power it on again.\n4. A dead backlight strip needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xtsp65lQnCc','2026-10-17 13:17:29.416000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.416000',4,618),(526,'Fix LG 22MP47 (2015): Monitor stays black','The LG 22MP47 (2015) powers on with an LED but shows no picture at all.','1. Press the input/source button to select the correct input.\n2. Reseat the video cable at both ends and try another cable.\n3. Test the monitor on another PC or plug in a different display.\n4. A dead power board or backlight needs repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZP-88Fx3eQ8','2026-10-17 13:17:29.431000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.431000',4,619),(527,'Fix Gigabyte P34G (2014): Not charging / no power light','The Gigabyte P34G (2014) shows no charging LED and does not power on with the adapter connected.','1. Test the adapter on another laptop and check the pin for damage.\n2. Unplug the battery, hold Power for 30 seconds, then reconnect everything.\n3. Try a different wall outlet and inspect the DC jack for looseness.\n4. A loose jack or dead board needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tBEzNUsmHQQ','2026-10-17 13:17:29.457000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.457000',4,620),(528,'Fix Gigabyte P55W (2015): Fan noise and overheating','The Gigabyte P55W (2015) runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=80WHnovW53c','2026-10-17 13:17:29.481000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.481000',4,621),(529,'Fix Gigabyte U2442 (2013): Extremely slow boot and apps','The Gigabyte U2442 (2013) takes many minutes to boot and applications hang constantly.','1. Run Disk Cleanup and remove startup programs you do not need.\n2. Check Task Manager for a drive stuck at 100 percent use.\n3. Scan for malware with up-to-date antivirus software.\n4. The biggest fix on older laptops is swapping the HDD for an SSD.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CcFY5GTdbIk','2026-10-17 13:17:29.497000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.497000',4,622),(530,'Fix Gigabyte Aero 14 (2017): Keyboard or trackpad not responding','Some keys on the Gigabyte Aero 14 (2017) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with compressed air.\n2. Reinstall or update the touchpad and chipset drivers.\n3. Plug in an external keyboard to see if the fault is hardware.\n4. Replace the keyboard assembly if keys stay dead.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ud0zMCBbpjk','2026-10-17 13:17:29.513000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.513000',4,623),(531,'Fix Gigabyte Aero 15 (2018): Not charging / no power light','The Gigabyte Aero 15 (2018) shows no charging LED and does not power on with the adapter connected.','1. Test the adapter on another laptop and check the pin for damage.\n2. Unplug the battery, hold Power for 30 seconds, then reconnect everything.\n3. Try a different wall outlet and inspect the DC jack for looseness.\n4. A loose jack or dead board needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_74ffhF-itE','2026-10-17 13:17:29.536000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.536000',4,624),(532,'Fix Gigabyte Sabre 15 (2017): Fan noise and overheating','The Gigabyte Sabre 15 (2017) runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=80WHnovW53c','2026-10-17 13:17:29.553000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.553000',4,625),(533,'Fix Gigabyte P35X (2015): Extremely slow boot and apps','The Gigabyte P35X (2015) takes many minutes to boot and applications hang constantly.','1. Run Disk Cleanup and remove startup programs you do not need.\n2. Check Task Manager for a drive stuck at 100 percent use.\n3. Scan for malware with up-to-date antivirus software.\n4. The biggest fix on older laptops is swapping the HDD for an SSD.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4gpn6muqEsc','2026-10-17 13:17:29.578000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.578000',4,626),(534,'Fix Gigabyte Brix GB-BXi7-4770R (2013): Powers on but no display','The Gigabyte Brix GB-BXi7-4770R (2013) fans spin and lights come on, but the monitor stays black.','1. Reseat the RAM and the graphics card.\n2. Try a different video cable and input on the monitor.\n3. Clear CMOS by removing the battery for five minutes.\n4. Listen for beep codes - they identify the failed component.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m3Bqh_EdgvI','2026-10-17 13:17:29.601000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.601000',4,627),(535,'Fix Gigabyte Aivia Osmium (2012): Lag, ghosting or stutter','The Gigabyte Aivia Osmium (2012) hesitates, jumps or stops responding for a moment.','1. Use the direct port on the back of the PC, not the front panel.\n2. Remove old drivers and install the latest one.\n3. Disconnect other USB devices, especially USB 3.0 hard drives.\n4. Replace the cable or battery if the device is wireless.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6oVD_eJU78k','2026-10-17 13:17:29.626000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.626000',4,628),(536,'Fix Gigabyte Aivia M8000 (2010): Keys or buttons not responding','Some keys on the Gigabyte Aivia M8000 (2010) need repeated presses or never register.','1. Clean under the keycaps with compressed air.\n2. Try the device on another computer.\n3. Disable sticky keys and filter keys in accessibility settings.\n4. Replace the key switch or membrane sheet if cleaning fails.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=88QKDRB_kY4','2026-10-17 13:17:29.658000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.658000',4,629),(537,'Fix MSI GT70 (2013): Keyboard or trackpad not responding','Some keys on the MSI GT70 (2013) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with compressed air.\n2. Reinstall or u