ng','Some keys on the MSI Prestige PE60 (2016) stop working or the cursor jumps without input.','1. Clean between the keys with compressed air.\n2. Reinstall or update the touchpad and chipset drivers.\n3. Plug in an external keyboard to see if the fault is hardware.\n4. Replace the keyboard assembly if keys stay dead.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FlOi7m1dDm4','2026-10-17 13:17:29.868000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.870000',4,638),(546,'Fix MSI Trident 3 (2017): Blue screen or boot loop','The MSI Trident 3 (2017) crashes with a stop error or repairs itself in a loop at startup.','1. Boot from installation media and run startup repair.\n2. Open the command prompt and run chkdsk /f /r.\n3. Test the RAM with the Windows memory diagnostic.\n4. Back up data and reinstall Windows if the drive is failing.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MKgCOlaIBdg','2026-10-17 13:17:29.893000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.893000',4,639),(547,'Fix Razer Blade 14 (2014): Not charging / no power light','The Razer Blade 14 (2014) shows no charging LED and does not power on with the adapter connected.','1. Test the adapter on another laptop and check the pin for damage.\n2. Unplug the battery, hold Power for 30 seconds, then reconnect everything.\n3. Try a different wall outlet and inspect the DC jack for looseness.\n4. A loose jack or dead board needs a technician repair.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PUoUVTXuhdU','2026-10-17 13:17:29.914000','2026-10-17 13:17:29.916000',4,640),(548,'Fix Razer Blade Stealth 13 (2016): Fan noise and overheating','The Razer Blade Stealth 13 (2016) runs loud, gets hot near the vents and throttles under load.','1. Clear the vents with compressed air and never block them on a bed or pillow.\n2. Use a cooling pad and raise the rear of the laptop.\n3. Open the base and replace the dried thermal paste.\n4. Replace the fan if the bearing rattles.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v5hMU5ZHaCY','2026-10-17 13:17:29.945000','2026-10-17 13:17