553,'Fix Razer Sabertooth (2013): Double clicks on a single press','The Razer Sabertooth (2013) registers two clicks or scrolls the wrong way.','1. Clean around the buttons and the scroll wheel with compressed air.\n2. Test in another application to confirm it is hardware.\n3. Toggle single or double click speed in mouse settings.\n4. Replace the microswitches or the unit if cleaning fails.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6pei7ytkIb8','2026-10-17 13:17:30.056000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.056000',4,646),(554,'Fix Razer Kraken 7.1 (2014): Distortion at higher volume','The Razer Kraken 7.1 (2014) crackles or sounds muffled when the volume goes up.','1. Lower the source volume and disable any equaliser boosts.\n2. Clean the speaker grille and check for a torn driver surround.\n3. Test on a second device to confirm it is not the source.\n4. A blown driver needs replacement.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dpYGU55tAJM','2026-10-17 13:17:30.079000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.079000',4,647),(555,'Fix Razer Seiren X (2017): Sound only in one ear','One side of the Razer Seiren X (2017) is silent or cuts in and out when the cable moves.','1. Clean the driver mesh and ear tips of wax and debris.\n2. Test another device to confirm the fault follows the earbuds.\n3. On wired models, bend the cable near the jack - a drop means a broken wire.\n4. For true wireless, put both buds in the case and reset them.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V1e6DbnLiv0','2026-10-17 13:17:30.099000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.099000',4,648),(556,'Fix Razer Nabu Watch (2015): Battery no longer holds a charge','The Razer Nabu Watch (2015) runs for less than a few hours and dies before the end of the day.','1. Reduce screen brightness and disable always-on display.\n2. Turn off 24/7 heart rate monitoring and GPS when unused.\n3. Clean the charging pins and reseat it on the dock.\n4. Batteries age - replace the unit or cell if capacity is below 60%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=binU7JLp32Q','2026-10-17 13:17:30.118000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.118000',4,649),(557,'Fix RedMagic Mars (2018): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The RedMagic Mars (2018) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xXVIzlvWtcA','2026-10-17 13:17:30.135000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.135000',4,650),(558,'Fix RedMagic 3 (2019): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the RedMagic 3 (2019) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OHsYgoyntlc','2026-10-17 13:17:30.160000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.160000',4,651),(559,'Fix RedMagic 3S (2019): Overheating while charging','The RedMagic 3S (2019) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GoZrVldnznw','2026-10-17 13:17:30.178000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.178000',4,652),(560,'Fix RedMagic 5G (2020): Battery drains quickly','The RedMagic 5G (2020) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uGQYmBaSCuE','2026-10-17 13:17:30.203000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.203000',4,653),(561,'Fix RedMagic 5S (2020): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The RedMagic 5S (2020) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xXVIzlvWtcA','2026-10-17 13:17:30.229000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.229000',4,654),(562,'Fix RedMagic 6 (2021): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the RedMagic 6 (2021) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OHsYgoyntlc','2026-10-17 13:17:30.259000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.259000',4,655),(563,'Fix RedMagic 6R (2021): Overheating while charging','The RedMagic 6R (2021) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GoZrVldnznw','2026-10-17 13:17:30.276000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.276000',4,656),(564,'Fix RedMagic 6S Pro (2021): Battery drains quickly','The RedMagic 6S Pro (2021) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2xGLm_jIxX4','2026-10-17 13:17:30.293000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.293000',4,657),(565,'Fix RedMagic 7 (2022): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The RedMagic 7 (2022) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=56_57McE4R8','2026-10-17 13:17:30.328000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.328000',4,658),(566,'Fix RedMagic Watch (2021): Charger not recognised','The RedMagic Watch (2021) does not light up or charge on its original dock.','1. Clean the magnetic contacts and pins with a dry cloth.\n2. Try a different USB cable and a phone charger, not a laptop port.\n3. Reset the watch while it is on the charger.\n4. Replace the dock if the cable tests fine elsewhere.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R9i1gfeWqJw','2026-10-17 13:17:30.345000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.345000',4,659),(567,'Fix Canon EOS 40D (2007): Photos come out blurry','Every shot from the Canon EOS 40D (2007) is soft or smeared, even in good light.','1. Clean the front element with a lens cloth.\n2. Switch the focus mode and use a single centre focus point.\n3. Check the shutter speed and raise ISO if it is too slow to hand-hold.\n4. A misaligned or jammed lens assembly needs service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dk0v_-5Edmg','2026-10-17 13:17:30.368000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.368000',4,660),(568,'Fix Canon EOS 1100D (2011): Will not power on','The Canon EOS 1100D (2011) is completely dead with batteries or the pack fitted.','1. Test the batteries in another device or use a fresh set.\n2. Clean the battery contacts with a dry cloth.\n3. Remove the battery for five minutes, reinsert and try again.\n4. Check the power board if the camera stays dead.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=234PBIs29jA','2026-10-17 13:17:30.395000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.395000',4,661),(569,'Fix Canon EOS 600D (2011): Memory card not recognised','The Canon EOS 600D (2011) reports no card, cannot format or refuses to save images.','1. Try another card - older cameras cap out at 32GB and Class 10.\n2. Slide the card lock switch to unlocked.\n3. Format the card inside the camera, not on a computer.\n4. Clean the card pins in the slot.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j_XihJ9Vjok','2026-10-17 13:17:30.421000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.421000',4,662),(570,'Fix Canon EOS 700D (2013): Stuck shutter or ERR message','The Canon EOS 700D (2013) shows an error code or the shutter stops responding.','1. Remove and reinsert the battery to clear the error.\n2. Switch to an empty lens mount and test the body.\n3. Do not force the lens - power down and start again.\n4. Shutter mechanisms need a technician after very high shot counts.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sjcNzA1n5Tc','2026-10-17 13:17:30.444000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.444000',4,663),(571,'Fix Canon EOS 750D (2015): Photos come out blurry','Every shot from the Canon EOS 750D (2015) is soft or smeared, even in good light.','1. Clean the front element with a lens cloth.\n2. Switch the focus mode and use a single centre focus point.\n3. Check the shutter speed and raise ISO if it is too slow to hand-hold.\n4. A misaligned or jammed lens assembly needs service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dk0v_-5Edmg','2026-10-17 13:17:30.472000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.472000',4,664),(572,'Fix Canon PowerShot G12 (2010): Will not power on','The Canon PowerShot G12 (2010) is completely dead with batteries or the pack fitted.','1. Test the batteries in another device or use a fresh set.\n2. Clean the battery contacts with a dry cloth.\n3. Remove the battery for five minutes, reinsert and try again.\n4. Check the power board if the camera stays dead.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=234PBIs29jA','2026-10-17 13:17:30.495000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.495000',4,665),(573,'Fix Canon PowerShot SX50 HS (2013): Memory card not recognised','The Canon PowerShot SX50 HS (2013) reports no card, cannot format or refuses to save images.','1. Try another card - older cameras cap out at 32GB and Class 10.\n2. Slide the card lock switch to unlocked.\n3. Format the card inside the camera, not on a computer.\n4. Clean the card pins in the slot.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KncuKVtwU34','2026-10-17 13:17:30.522000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.522000',4,666),(574,'Fix Canon IXUS 220 HS (2011): Stuck shutter or ERR message','The Canon IXUS 220 HS (2011) shows an error code or the shutter stops responding.','1. Remove and reinsert the battery to clear the error.\n2. Switch to an empty lens mount and test the body.\n3. Do not force the lens - power down and start again.\n4. Shutter mechanisms need a technician after very high shot counts.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZBmpkwmiMfo','2026-10-17 13:17:30.546000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.546000',4,667),(575,'Fix Canon PIXMA MG2570 (2014): Will not connect to Wi-Fi','The Canon PIXMA MG2570 (2014) drops off the network or will not join it at all.','1. Print a network configuration page and check the signal.\n2. Reconnect from the printer panel using WPS or the Wi-Fi Setup menu.\n3. Keep the printer within range of the router on 2.4GHz.\n4. Reinstall the driver and print a test page from the PC.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Ge11VfqJnQ','2026-10-17 13:17:30.563000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.563000',4,668),(576,'Fix Canon PIXMA iP2770 (2010): Streaks after a new cartridge','Printouts from the Canon PIXMA iP2770 (2010) show bands right after a cartridge change.','1. Remove the cartridge and peel off the orange protective tape.\n2. Wipe the electrical contacts with a dry lint-free cloth.\n3. Reseat the cartridge until it clicks and run cleaning twice.\n4. Align the print head from the printer software.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pAUZ9lLzpmw','2026-10-17 13:17:30.579000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.579000',4,669),(577,'Fix Epson L110 (2013): Paper keeps jamming','Every job on the Epson L110 (2013) jams or pulls in multiple sheets at once.','1. Remove the paper, fan the stack and reload below the tray limit.\n2. Pull out all sheets and check the tray for torn paper fragments.\n3. Clean the rubber pickup roller with a damp cloth.\n4. Adjust the paper guides firmly against the stack.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SNvq4cB2-UY','2026-10-17 13:17:30.602000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.602000',4,670),(578,'Fix Epson L355 (2014): Prints are faded or streaked','Output from the Epson L355 (2014) has grey text, white bands or missing colours.','1. Run the built-in nozzle check / print quality report.\n2. Run the head cleaning cycle up to three times from the driver.\n3. Replace low or dried-out cartridges.\n4. On ink tank models, shake the bottle and refill the empty tank.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yFVpvAUeneA','2026-10-17 13:17:30.620000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.620000',4,671),(579,'Fix Epson Stylus T13 (2011): Will not connect to Wi-Fi','The Epson Stylus T13 (2011) drops off the network or will not join it at all.','1. Print a network configuration page and check the signal.\n2. Reconnect from the printer panel using WPS or the Wi-Fi Setup menu.\n3. Keep the printer within range of the router on 2.4GHz.\n4. Reinstall the driver and print a test page from the PC.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cKNRvHRsg6I','2026-10-17 13:17:30.640000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.640000',4,672),(580,'Fix Epson L360 (2016): Streaks after a new cartridge','Printouts from the Epson L360 (2016) show bands right after a cartridge change.','1. Remove the cartridge and peel off the orange protective tape.\n2. Wipe the electrical contacts with a dry lint-free cloth.\n3. Reseat the cartridge until it clicks and run cleaning twice.\n4. Align the print head from the printer software.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-5pJ_Hbm0O8','2026-10-17 13:17:30.661000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.661000',4,673),(581,'Fix Epson Expression Home XP-220 (2015): Paper keeps jamming','Every job on the Epson Expression Home XP-220 (2015) jams or pulls in multiple sheets at once.','1. Remove the paper, fan the stack and reload below the tray limit.\n2. Pull out all sheets and check the tray for torn paper fragments.\n3. Clean the rubber pickup roller with a damp cloth.\n4. Adjust the paper guides firmly against the stack.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jXUNIadlfns','2026-10-17 13:17:30.678000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.678000',4,674),(582,'Fix Epson WorkForce WF-2630 (2015): Prints are faded or streaked','Output from the Epson WorkForce WF-2630 (2015) has grey text, white bands or missing colours.','1. Run the built-in nozzle check / print quality report.\n2. Run the head cleaning cycle up to three times from the driver.\n3. Replace low or dried-out cartridges.\n4. On ink tank models, shake the bottle and refill the empty tank.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jkrIznMQFro','2026-10-17 13:17:30.702000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.702000',4,675),(583,'Fix Epson L120 (2014): Will not connect to Wi-Fi','The Epson L120 (2014) drops off the network or will not join it at all.','1. Print a network configuration page and check the signal.\n2. Reconnect from the printer panel using WPS or the Wi-Fi Setup menu.\n3. Keep the printer within range of the router on 2.4GHz.\n4. Reinstall the driver and print a test page from the PC.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZqRLkgx3W2Y','2026-10-17 13:17:30.720000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.720000',4,676),(584,'Fix Epson Perfection V37 Scanner (2011): Lag, ghosting or stutter','The Epson Perfection V37 Scanner (2011) hesitates, jumps or stops responding for a moment.','1. Use the direct port on the back of the PC, not the front panel.\n2. Remove old drivers and install the latest one.\n3. Disconnect other USB devices, especially USB 3.0 hard drives.\n4. Replace the cable or battery if the device is wireless.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b--Mb_2s59s','2026-10-17 13:17:30.734000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.734000',4,677),(585,'Fix Epson Perfection V600 Scanner (2009): Keys or buttons not responding','Some keys on the Epson Perfection V600 Scanner (2009) need repeated presses or never register.','1. Clean under the keycaps with compressed air.\n2. Try the device on another computer.\n3. Disable sticky keys and filter keys in accessibility settings.\n4. Replace the key switch or membrane sheet if cleaning fails.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b--Mb_2s59s','2026-10-17 13:17:30.764000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.764000',4,678),(586,'Fix Epson PowerLite 84 (2010): Device not detected','The Epson PowerLite 84 (2010) does not show up on the computer at all.','1. Plug it into another USB port, avoiding hubs and pass-throughs.\n2. Test it on a second computer.\n3. Reinstall the driver from Device Manager > Uninstall device.\n4. Replace the cable if it is detachable.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XRhqzWY_uFA','2026-10-17 13:17:30.775000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.775000',4,679),(587,'Fix TP-Link TL-WR841N (2012): Very slow or weak signal','The TP-Link TL-WR841N (2012) coverage is poor and speed drops in other rooms.','1. Move the router to a central, elevated position away from walls.\n2. Switch to a clear channel - use 1, 6 or 11 on 2.4GHz.\n3. Remove old cordless phone and microwave interference.\n4. Add a range extender or mesh node for distant rooms.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDtA0OKbx_Q','2026-10-17 13:17:30.804000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.804000',4,680),(588,'Fix TP-Link TL-WR740N (2011): Cannot open the admin page','Browsing to the TP-Link TL-WR740N (2011) setup address times out or asks for a wrong password.','1. Connect by cable or to the default SSID first.\n2. Try the default IP printed on the router label, not a website name.\n3. Disable VPN and proxy settings, then clear the browser cache.\n4. Hold reset for 10 seconds to restore factory settings.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j9V3vNttnhw','2026-10-17 13:17:30.827000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.827000',4,681),(589,'Fix TP-Link Archer C5 (2014): Keeps dropping connection','The TP-Link Archer C5 (2014) randomly disconnects every few minutes across all devices.','1. Update the router firmware from the admin page.\n2. Reduce the number of connected devices and disable unused bands.\n3. Change the Wi-Fi channel and set a fixed 2.4GHz channel width.\n4. Replace the unit if it restarts on its own - that signals a power fault.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lQ0Hu12p1cY','2026-10-17 13:17:30.847000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.847000',4,682),(590,'Fix TP-Link Archer C7 (2013): No internet but Wi-Fi is connected','Devices join the TP-Link Archer C7 (2013) network but pages will not load.','1. Restart the modem and the router in that order.\n2. Check that the WAN cable is plugged into the correct port.\n3. Release and renew the IP address on the affected device.\n4. Reset the router to factory defaults if the modem line is fine.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gnMXMYyH3g4','2026-10-17 13:17:30.874000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.874000',4,683),(591,'Fix TP-Link TL-WR941ND (2013): Very slow or weak signal','The TP-Link TL-WR941ND (2013) coverage is poor and speed drops in other rooms.','1. Move the router to a central, elevated position away from walls.\n2. Switch to a clear channel - use 1, 6 or 11 on 2.4GHz.\n3. Remove old cordless phone and microwave interference.\n4. Add a range extender or mesh node for distant rooms.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7BYxS_bg07I','2026-10-17 13:17:30.893000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.893000',4,684),(592,'Fix TP-Link TL-MR3420 (2013): Cannot open the admin page','Browsing to the TP-Link TL-MR3420 (2013) setup address times out or asks for a wrong password.','1. Connect by cable or to the default SSID first.\n2. Try the default IP printed on the router label, not a website name.\n3. Disable VPN and proxy settings, then clear the browser cache.\n4. Hold reset for 10 seconds to restore factory settings.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=trAm0_NZ_Ok','2026-10-17 13:17:30.914000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.914000',4,685),(593,'Fix TP-Link TL-WA850RE (2014): Keeps dropping connection','The TP-Link TL-WA850RE (2014) randomly disconnects every few minutes across all devices.','1. Update the router firmware from the admin page.\n2. Reduce the number of connected devices and disable unused bands.\n3. Change the Wi-Fi channel and set a fixed 2.4GHz channel width.\n4. Replace the unit if it restarts on its own - that signals a power fault.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tOZcDt3aRRg','2026-10-17 13:17:30.949000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.949000',4,686),(594,'Fix TP-Link Deco M5 (2017): No internet but Wi-Fi is connected','Devices join the TP-Link Deco M5 (2017) network but pages will not load.','1. Restart the modem and the router in that order.\n2. Check that the WAN cable is plugged into the correct port.\n3. Release and renew the IP address on the affected device.\n4. Reset the router to factory defaults if the modem line is fine.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6_II49JKJDc','2026-10-17 13:17:30.963000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.963000',4,687),(595,'Fix TP-Link Neffos C5 (2016): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the TP-Link Neffos C5 (2016) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8AY5RUTSnHc','2026-10-17 13:17:30.984000','2026-10-17 13:17:30.984000',4,688),(596,'Fix TP-Link Neffos Y5L (2016): Overheating while charging','The TP-Link Neffos Y5L (2016) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=73cOw5bEcy8','2026-10-17 13:17:31.003000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.003000',4,689),(597,'Fix Anker PowerCore 10000 (2016): Charging very slowly or not at all','The Anker PowerCore 10000 (2016) charges devices far slower than rated or not at all.','1. Use a wall outlet, not a laptop USB port.\n2. Clean lint and dust from the device\'s charging port.\n3. Try a known-good cable to confirm which side is at fault.\n4. Stop using the charger if it is hot, swollen or smells burnt.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y16Im50Oitg','2026-10-17 13:17:31.019000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.019000',4,690),(598,'Fix Anker PowerCore 5000 (2015): Device not recognised when connected','Plugging in with the Anker PowerCore 5000 (2015) gives no reaction or a \'not recognised\' error.','1. Reseat the connector - push it in fully until it clicks.\n2. Try the other direction for reversible connectors and another cable.\n3. Restart the device and test the port for bent pins or debris.\n4. Replace the cable if the port works with other leads.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e_w3UNrdcEY','2026-10-17 13:17:31.037000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.037000',4,691),(599,'Fix Anker PowerCore 20100 (2016): Connector loose or sparking','The Anker PowerCore 20100 (2016) falls out of the port or crackles while charging.','1. Stop using the cable - a loose connection can overheat the port.\n2. Inspect the tip for bent pins, fraying or exposed wire.\n3. Straighten a bent tip carefully or cut off a frayed end.\n4. Replace the cable or charger - do not repair it with tape.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e_w3UNrdcEY','2026-10-17 13:17:31.058000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.058000',4,692),(600,'Fix Anker PowerCore+ 26800 (2016): Power bank will not charge','The Anker PowerCore+ 26800 (2016) does not accept a charge or its LEDs flash and stop.','1. Hold the power button for 10 seconds to wake the circuit.\n2. Use a 2A adapter and a good cable - thin cables starve big banks.\n3. Clean the ports and let it charge uninterrupted for one hour.\n4. Deeply discharged cells may be beyond recovery and need replacing.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t0vsQ2MxeHM','2026-10-17 13:17:31.080000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.080000',4,693),(601,'Fix Anker PowerPort 4 (2016): Charging very slowly or not at all','The Anker PowerPort 4 (2016) charges devices far slower than rated or not at all.','1. Use a wall outlet, not a laptop USB port.\n2. Clean lint and dust from the device\'s charging port.\n3. Try a known-good cable to confirm which side is at fault.\n4. Stop using the charger if it is hot, swollen or smells burnt.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y16Im50Oitg','2026-10-17 13:17:31.094000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.094000',4,694),(602,'Fix Anker PowerPort Atom PD1 (2019): Device not recognised when connected','Plugging in with the Anker PowerPort Atom PD1 (2019) gives no reaction or a \'not recognised\' error.','1. Reseat the connector - push it in fully until it clicks.\n2. Try the other direction for reversible connectors and another cable.\n3. Restart the device and test the port for bent pins or debris.\n4. Replace the cable if the port works with other leads.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-UXA7aDHdbM','2026-10-17 13:17:31.117000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.117000',4,695),(603,'Fix Anker SoundCore 2 (2017): Will not hold a charge','The Anker SoundCore 2 (2017) dies within minutes even after a full charge cycle.','1. Clean the charging contacts with a dry cotton swab.\n2. Leave it on charge for 30 minutes before use and use a 5V adapter.\n3. Update the firmware from the companion app.\n4. Old cells fade - battery replacement or a new unit is the fix.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6YnVn-xZBI0','2026-10-17 13:17:31.145000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.145000',4,696),(604,'Fix Anker SoundBuds Slim (2017): Pairing fails or drops','The Anker SoundBuds Slim (2017) disappears from the device list or will not complete pairing.','1. Forget the device on the phone, then restart both devices.\n2. Clear the pairing list on the headphones and pair again.\n3. Move away from Wi-Fi routers and USB 3.0 hubs that cause interference.\n4. Update the app and firmware to the latest version.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vQOw7z1Hx2g','2026-10-17 13:17:31.159000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.159000',4,697),(605,'Fix Anker SoundCore Sport XL (2016): Distortion at higher volume','The Anker SoundCore Sport XL (2016) crackles or sounds muffled when the volume goes up.','1. Lower the source volume and disable any equaliser boosts.\n2. Clean the speaker grille and check for a torn driver surround.\n3. Test on a second device to confirm it is not the source.\n4. A blown driver needs replacement.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KzgY2Vvk36Q','2026-10-17 13:17:31.178000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.178000',4,698),(606,'Fix Anker Roav C1 (2016): Photos come out blurry','Every shot from the Anker Roav C1 (2016) is soft or smeared, even in good light.','1. Clean the front element with a lens cloth.\n2. Switch the focus mode and use a single centre focus point.\n3. Check the shutter speed and raise ISO if it is too slow to hand-hold.\n4. A misaligned or jammed lens assembly needs service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeYetkYMXs','2026-10-17 13:17:31.193000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.193000',4,699),(607,'Fix Baseus 65W GaN Charger (2019): Connector loose or sparking','The Baseus 65W GaN Cha