ther device to confirm the fault follows the earbuds.\n3. On wired models, bend the cable near the jack - a drop means a broken wire.\n4. For true wireless, put both buds in the case and reset them.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ny3aNoYrj2s','2026-10-17 13:17:31.983000','2026-10-17 13:17:31.983000',4,738),(646,'Fix JBL Playlist Speaker (2016): Will not hold a charge','The JBL Playlist Speaker (2016) dies within minutes even after a full charge cycle.','1. Clean the charging contacts with a dry cotton swab.\n2. Leave it on charge for 30 minutes before use and use a 5V adapter.\n3. Update the firmware from the companion app.\n4. Old cells fade - battery replacement or a new unit is the fix.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKjcca6Zi6k','2026-10-17 13:17:32.001000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.001000',4,739),(647,'Fix Sony Xperia Z3 (2014): Battery drains quickly','The Sony Xperia Z3 (2014) loses its charge within a few hours of light use and shuts down unexpectedly below 20%.','1. Open Settings > Battery and check which apps use the most power.\n2. Lower screen brightness and disable location services for unused apps.\n3. Boot to Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n4. If battery health is under 80%, replace the cell - old batteries need service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZfbpdgmc3s','2026-10-17 13:17:32.013000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.013000',4,740),(648,'Fix Sony Xperia Z5 (2015): Stuck on the boot logo / restart loop','The Sony Xperia Z5 (2015) freezes on the brand logo or keeps rebooting and never reaches the home screen.','1. Force restart by holding Power + Volume Down for 10 seconds.\n2. Boot into Recovery mode and wipe the cache partition.\n3. Back up what you can, then do a factory reset.\n4. If the loop returns, reflash the firmware with the brand desktop tool.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XLgKW_8sF8Q','2026-10-17 13:17:32.032000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.032000',4,741),(649,'Fix Sony Xperia M4 Aqua (2015): Touchscreen dead zones','Parts of the Sony Xperia M4 Aqua (2015) screen ignore taps or respond late, usually after a drop or moisture exposure.','1. Remove the screen protector and case, then clean the glass.\n2. Restart the phone and test again.\n3. Boot into Safe Mode to rule out a rogue app.\n4. Run the hardware test code; if it fails, replace the display assembly.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FAIhwZHfzl4','2026-10-17 13:17:32.048000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.048000',4,742),(650,'Fix Sony Xperia L (2013): Overheating while charging','The Sony Xperia L (2013) gets very hot during charging or camera use and slows down.','1. Use only the original charger and cable.\n2. Remove the case while charging and keep it out of direct sun.\n3. Close background apps and install the latest software update.\n4. Persistent heat means the charging board or battery needs checking.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YcsIdmF8qko','2026-10-17 13:17:32.064000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.064000',4,743),(651,'Fix Sony WH-1000XM2 (2017): Pairing fails or drops','The Sony WH-1000XM2 (2017) disappears from the device list or will not complete pairing.','1. Forget the device on the phone, then restart both devices.\n2. Clear the pairing list on the headphones and pair again.\n3. Move away from Wi-Fi routers and USB 3.0 hubs that cause interference.\n4. Update the app and firmware to the latest version.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ASHMAwe7rXg','2026-10-17 13:17:32.076000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.076000',4,744),(652,'Fix Sony MDR-EX155 In-Ear Earphones (2014): Distortion at higher volume','The Sony MDR-EX155 In-Ear Earphones (2014) crackles or sounds muffled when the volume goes up.','1. Lower the source volume and disable any equaliser boosts.\n2. Clean the speaker grille and check for a torn driver surround.\n3. Test on a second device to confirm it is not the source.\n4. A blown driver needs replacement.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eUB3XPOuf-o','2026-10-17 13:17:32.088000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.088000',4,745),(653,'Fix Sony Alpha a5100 (2014): Will not power on','The Sony Alpha a5100 (2014) is completely dead with batteries or the pack fitted.','1. Test the batteries in another device or use a fresh set.\n2. Clean the battery contacts with a dry cloth.\n3. Remove the battery for five minutes, reinsert and try again.\n4. Check the power board if the camera stays dead.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xh7iDtmpedc','2026-10-17 13:17:32.101000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.101000',4,746),(654,'Fix Sony Alpha a6000 (2014): Memory card not recognised','The Sony Alpha a6000 (2014) reports no card, cannot format or refuses to save images.','1. Try another card - older cameras cap out at 32GB and Class 10.\n2. Slide the card lock switch to unlocked.\n3. Format the card inside the camera, not on a computer.\n4. Clean the card pins in the slot.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c6rLkdxnh1M','2026-10-17 13:17:32.117000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.117000',4,747),(655,'Fix Sony PlayStation Vita (2011): Buttons or sticks drifting','Characters move or menus jump without touching the Sony PlayStation Vita (2011) controls.','1. Recalibrate the stick from the settings menu.\n2. Clean around the stick with compressed air and isopropyl alcohol.\n3. Update the firmware and test in the built-in diagnostic screen.\n4. Replace the stick module if drift remains.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Uwkho7wZa4Y','2026-10-17 13:17:32.129000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.129000',4,748),(656,'Fix Sony KDL-40R355 (2014): Apps freeze or crash','Apps on the Sony KDL-40R355 (2014) hang, crash back to the home screen or never load.','1. Clear the app cache and data from settings.\n2. Uninstall and reinstall the failing app.\n3. Update the TV firmware from Settings > Support.\n4. As a last resort, reset the TV to factory settings.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZVgfetVe-oc','2026-10-17 13:17:32.144000','2026-10-17 13:17:32.144000',4,749);
